    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The project has a single test \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: on successful owner create, enqueue a welcome notification by emitting a line via the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I mirrored the codebase's established pattern (each create-flow rule is a small, self-contained policy class invoked from the controller):\n\n1. **New class** `service/OwnerWelcomeNotificationPolicy.java` \u2014 a tiny, cohesive unit with a single method `enqueueWelcome(Owner)` that logs via the `NOTIFY` logger. As a fresh class its `WMC_other` is 0 and its method's CC is 1.\n\n2. **One line added** to `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, placed after `saveOwner` (so `owner.getId()` is populated) and after `auditCreate`, plus one import line.\n\nNo existing method grew in complexity; the only edit to a large class is a single call line. Verified output: `INFO NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
